 - [outer-loop] Wrote `results/operational_retro_2026_06_366.json` (schema `carnot.operational_retro.v64`). Authoritative timing reports no experiment commits since activation of 2026.06.366: `total_wall_time_minutes=0`, `experiments_completed=0`, `compute_bound_experiments_count=0`, `slowest_experiments=[]`, `gpu_idle_on_compute_bound_tasks=null`. Both RTX 3090s idle is correct (0 compute-bound tasks) and is NOT flagged as a bottleneck. KEY FINDING: this is the third consecutive zero-commit retro (.363/.365/.366) while `ops/changelog.md` shows completed experiment activity in the same windows — pointing at a commit-range attribution/timing gap in the retro's milestone-scoped commit detector rather than genuinely empty milestones. Highest-leverage fix: audit the detector and add a `detector_undercount_suspected` self-check (0 commits found AND `results/experiment_*.json` present in window).
